# No em dashes (compulsory)

Em dashes (`—`), en dashes (`–`), minus signs (`−`), and HTML entities (`&mdash;`, `&ndash;`) are forbidden in this project. They read as AI-generated and must never appear in HTML served to users or crawlers.

## Required behavior

- Never type `—`, `–`, or `−` in copy, UI strings, comments meant for users, MDX, CMS seeds, SEO metadata, or design-system docs.
- Use a normal hyphen with spaces instead: ` - `
  - Bad: `future — how it grows`
  - Good: `future - how it grows`
- Prefer commas, periods, or parentheses when a hyphen feels awkward.
- Empty admin placeholders use `"-"` (ASCII hyphen), never an em dash.
- When editing or generating content, strip these characters before committing.
- Public/CMS text still runs through `lib/content/strip-em-dashes.ts` on save and render - that is a safety net, not permission to introduce dashes in source.

## Do not

- Do not hide dashes with CSS.
- Do not leave them in source "because runtime strips them."
- Do not reintroduce them in homepage/static `content/*` files.

## Quick check

Before finishing copy or UI text work, search the diff for `—` / `–` and remove any matches.
